# The bundle of the init harness on x86-64: the objects the bootloader loads
# from \EFI\seraph\bootstrap.bundle (docs/boot-media.md § The ESP). Each line
# names an installed file by its install path, which is also its entry's name;
# the `init` line names the object of the `init` slot. A pack copies each
# file into the bundle byte for byte, and signs each entry but `init` in the
# role the bootloader verifies it in: configuration under `/config/` (a platform
# table excepted), boot module otherwise.
#
# Only the bootstrap closure belongs here (docs/boot-media.md § The Bootstrap
# Closure): the block and filesystem drivers that read the root filesystem,
# and the services that bring userspace up to its mount. Every other driver,
# the consoles' included, and every platform description table is loaded from
# the root filesystem after the mount; an entry here costs memory that
# outlives the bootloader (step9_populate_boot_info, core/boot/src/main.rs).
init /services/init
/services/procmgr
/services/devmgr
/services/vfsd
/services/drivers/virtio-blk
/services/fs/fatfs
/services/memmgr
# The IOMMU driver, which devmgr spawns before the first DMA-capable driver.
/services/drivers/iommu-vtd
# The log-level configuration init reads at boot.
/config/init/log-levels.conf
# The boot-time policy devmgr reads before the first driver starts, which
# the bootloader requires of every bundle (docs/signing.md § Configuration).
/config/boot/policy.conf
